# OSRIP configuration overview. Placeholders only - never put real values in this file.
#
# Settings live in three places; copy the matching example and fill it in:
#   backend/.env   <- backend/.env.example   (API: database, sessions, model, search, speech)
#   frontend/.env  <- frontend/.env.example  (public build options only: no secrets, ever)
#   deploy/.env    <- deploy/.env.example    (production host: everything the containers need)
#
# Keys and passwords stay on the server. Anything named VITE_* is compiled into the public
# JavaScript bundle, so no key, token, secret or password may use that prefix.
#
# Optional services and the settings that switch them on (server side):
#   AI answers ........ OSRIP_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=<anthropic-api-key>
#   Web research ...... OSRIP_RESEARCH_API_KEY=<brave-search-api-key>
#   Voice ............. OSRIP_SPEECH_KEY=<azure-speech-key>  OSRIP_SPEECH_REGION=<azure-region>
#   E-mail ............ OSRIP_EMAIL_BACKEND=smtp  OSRIP_SMTP_HOST=<host> ...
#   Google sign-in .... OSRIP_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=<id>  OSRIP_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=<secret>
#   Microsoft sign-in . OSRIP_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=<id>  OSRIP_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET=<secret>
#   SMS ............... not available until a provider adapter is written (docs/INTEGRATIONS.md)
#
# Without a setting, the feature is shown as unavailable; nothing is simulated.
#
# One-off account creation (never stored in a file): set the password only in the
# terminal session, or let the command prompt for it:
#   OSRIP_NEW_USER_PASSWORD=<typed-in-terminal-only>
